      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','Left pass: maintain an increasing stack. For each `i`, pop while `heights[top] >= heights[i]`. `left[i]` is the new top, or `-1`. Push `i`.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.','Right pass: symmetric, from right to left. `right[i]` is the new top, or `n` if empty.','This step performs one part of the overall transformation. It prepares the state required by the following step and contributes to the final result.','Area for bar `i` is `heights[i] * (right[i] - left[i] - 1)`.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.'],
