      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','Merge `nums1` and `nums2` into `merged` (standard two-pointer merge).','This step performs one part of the overall transformation. It prepares the state required by the following step and contributes to the final result.','If the length is odd, return the middle element. Otherwise return the average of the two middle elements.','This is the decision point: evaluate the condition using the state built so far. Taking the correct branch prevents invalid work and keeps the algorithm aligned with the problem\'s constraints.'],
