    problemIntuition: 'Every path has a highest node, its apex, where it turns. At the apex, the path uses at most two downward branches. A branch with a negative sum is never worth taking, so clamp each branch\'s contribution at zero. The maximum path through a node is `node.val + max(0, leftGain) + max(0, rightGain)`. A post-order DFS can compute each node\'s best downward gain and update a global maximum with the apex value.',
