      intuition: 'Write nodes in BFS order, and write `#` for each missing child. To decode, read tokens in the same order with a queue, attaching each child slot to the next node in line.',
      algorithm: ['Serialize: BFS. For each dequeued node, append its value. If it has no left child, append `#`, otherwise enqueue it. Do the same for the right child. Join tokens with `,`.','Deserialize: split on `,`. Create the root from the first token. Enqueue it. For each dequeued node, read the next token for its left child and then for its right child. Create a node for any non-`#` token and enqueue it.'],
      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','Serialize: BFS. For each dequeued node, append its value. If it has no left child, append `#`, otherwise enqueue it. Do the same for the right child. Join tokens with `,`.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.','Deserialize: split on `,`. Create the root from the first token. Enqueue it. For each dequeued node, read the next token for its left child and then for its right child. Create a node for any non-`#` token and enqueue it.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.'],
      correctnessCheck: 'The solution is correct when the maintained state contains exactly the information required by the problem and every processed element has been handled according to the stated rule. The final step reads or constructs the answer from that state.',
      code: "import java.util.ArrayDeque;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Queue;\n\nclass Codec {\n    public String serialize(TreeNode root) {\n        if (root == null) return \"#\";\n        List<String> tokens = new ArrayList<>();\n        Queue<TreeNode> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();\n        queue.offer(root);\n        tokens.add(String.valueOf(root.val));\n        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {\n            TreeNode n = queue.poll();\n            for (TreeNode child : new TreeNode[]{n.left, n.right}) {\n                if (child == null) {\n                    tokens.add(\"#\");\n                } else {\n                    tokens.add(String.valueOf(child.val));\n                    queue.offer(child);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return String.join(\",\", tokens);\n    }\n\n    public TreeNode deserialize(String data) {\n        String[] t = data.split(\",\");\n        if (t[0].equals(\"#\")) return null;\n        TreeNode root = new TreeNode(Integer.parseInt(t[0]));\n        Queue<TreeNode> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();\n        queue.offer(root);\n        int i = 1;\n        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {\n            TreeNode n = queue.poll();\n            if (!t[i].equals(\"#\")) {\n                n.left = new TreeNode(Integer.parseInt(t[i]));\n                queue.offer(n.left);\n            }\n            i++;\n            if (!t[i].equals(\"#\")) {\n                n.right = new TreeNode(Integer.parseInt(t[i]));\n                queue.offer(n.right);\n            }\n            i++;\n        }\n        return root;\n    }\n}",
      pythonCode: undefined,
