      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','`select(lo, hi)`: pick a random pivot in `[lo, hi]`, swap it to `hi`, and partition by distance (Lomuto).','This changes the order or position of the data in a controlled way. That change makes the next operation simpler while preserving the information needed for the final answer.','If the pivot\'s final index `p` equals `k`, stop. If `p < k`, search `[p+1, hi]`. Otherwise search `[lo, p-1]`.','This is the decision point: evaluate the condition using the state built so far. Taking the correct branch prevents invalid work and keeps the algorithm aligned with the problem\'s constraints.','Return the first `k` points.','This produces the result after the required condition has been established. If the problem guarantees a solution, this final fallback may be unreachable; otherwise it represents the appropriate no-solution case.'],
      correctnessCheck: 'The solution is correct when the maintained state contains exactly the information required by the problem and every processed element has been handled according to the stated rule. The final step reads or constructs the answer from that state.',
      code: "import java.util.Arrays;\nimport java.util.Random;\n\nclass Solution {\n    private final Random rnd = new Random();\n\n    public int[][] kClosest(int[][] points, int k) {\n        select(points, 0, points.length - 1, k);\n        return Arrays.copyOf(points, k);\n    }\n\n    private void select(int[][] pts, int lo, int hi, int k) {\n        while (lo < hi) {\n            int r = lo + rnd.nextInt(hi - lo + 1);\n            swap(pts, r, hi);\n            int pivot = dist(pts[hi]);\n            int i = lo;\n            for (int j = lo; j < hi; j++) {\n                if (dist(pts[j]) < pivot) {\n                    swap(pts, i, j);\n                    i++;\n                }\n            }\n            swap(pts, i, hi);\n            if (i == k) return;\n            if (i < k) lo = i + 1;\n            else hi = i - 1;\n        }\n    }\n\n    private long dist(int[] p) {\n        return (long) p[0] * p[0] + (long) p[1] * p[1];\n    }\n\n    private void swap(int[][] a, int i, int j) {\n        int[] t = a[i];\n        a[i] = a[j];\n        a[j] = t;\n    }\n}",
