      label: 'Brute Force',
      intuition: 'Simulate cycle by cycle. Each cycle, choose the task with the highest remaining count among those whose cooldown has expired. If none is available, the cycle is idle.',
      algorithm: ['`cnt[26]` holds remaining counts, `readyAt[26]` holds the cycle when each task becomes available.','For `time = 0, 1, ...` until all tasks are done:','- Pick the available task with the highest count.','- If found, decrement its count, set `readyAt = time + n + 1`, and mark one task done.','- Advance `time`.','Return `time`.'],
      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','`cnt[26]` holds remaining counts, `readyAt[26]` holds the cycle when each task becomes available.','This step performs one part of the overall transformation. It prepares the state required by the following step and contributes to the final result.','For `time = 0, 1, ...` until all tasks are done:','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.','Return `time`.','This produces the result after the required condition has been established. If the problem guarantees a solution, this final fallback may be unreachable; otherwise it represents the appropriate no-solution case.'],
      correctnessCheck: 'The solution is correct when the maintained state contains exactly the information required by the problem and every processed element has been handled according to the stated rule. The final step reads or constructs the answer from that state.',
      code: "class Solution {\n    public int leastInterval(char[] tasks, int n) {\n        int[] cnt = new int[26], readyAt = new int[26];\n        for (char t : tasks) cnt[t - 'A']++;\n        int remaining = tasks.length, time = 0;\n        while (remaining > 0) {\n            int best = -1;\n            for (int c = 0; c < 26; c++) {\n                if (cnt[c] > 0 && readyAt[c] <= time && (best == -1 || cnt[c] > cnt[best])) {\n                    best = c;\n                }\n            }\n            if (best != -1) {\n                cnt[best]--;\n                readyAt[best] = time + n + 1;\n                remaining--;\n            }\n            time++;\n        }\n        return time;\n    }\n}",
