      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','For every start cell, run `dfs`.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.','`dfs`: check bounds, match, and not visited. If `idx` is the last character, return `true`.','This extracts the information needed to decide what to do next. The check connects the current input to the condition the problem asks us to satisfy.','Mark, explore the four neighbours, then unmark.','This updates the maintained state to include the current element or decision. Future iterations can then use that information instead of recomputing it.'],
