      label: 'Brute Force',
      intuition: 'Collect every original node in a list. Create a clone per node, in the same order. To wire the edges, find each neighbour\'s index in the list by linear search.',
      algorithm: ['DFS to collect all original nodes into `nodes`.','Create `clones[i] = new Node(nodes[i].val)`.','For each `i`, for each neighbour `nb`, find `j` with `nodes[j] == nb` by linear search, and add `clones[j]` to `clones[i].neighbors`.'],
      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','DFS to collect all original nodes into `nodes`.','This step performs one part of the overall transformation. It prepares the state required by the following step and contributes to the final result.','Create `clones[i] = new Node(nodes[i].val)`.','This prepares the data structure or state needed by later operations. Its initial value is important: it represents the fact that no elements or decisions have been processed yet.','For each `i`, for each neighbour `nb`, find `j` with `nodes[j] == nb` by linear search, and add `clones[j]` to `clones[i].neighbors`.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.'],
