      algorithm: ['Loop: copy the grid, rot every fresh orange adjacent to a rotten one (reading from the old grid), and track whether anything changed.','If nothing changed, stop. Count the minutes that changed something.','If any fresh orange remains, return `-1`.'],
      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','Loop: copy the grid, rot every fresh orange adjacent to a rotten one (reading from the old grid), and track whether anything changed.','This step performs one part of the overall transformation. It prepares the state required by the following step and contributes to the final result.','If nothing changed, stop. Count the minutes that changed something.','This is the decision point: evaluate the condition using the state built so far. Taking the correct branch prevents invalid work and keeps the algorithm aligned with the problem\'s constraints.','If any fresh orange remains, return `-1`.','This is the decision point: evaluate the condition using the state built so far. Taking the correct branch prevents invalid work and keeps the algorithm aligned with the problem\'s constraints.'],
      correctnessCheck: 'The solution is correct when the maintained state contains exactly the information required by the problem and every processed element has been handled according to the stated rule. The final step reads or constructs the answer from that state.',
      code: "class Solution {\n    public int orangesRotting(int[][] grid) {\n        int m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length, minutes = 0;\n        int[][] g = new int[m][];\n        for (int r = 0; r < m; r++) g[r] = grid[r].clone();\n        while (true) {\n            int[][] next = new int[m][];\n            for (int r = 0; r < m; r++) next[r] = g[r].clone();\n            boolean changed = false;\n            for (int r = 0; r < m; r++) {\n                for (int c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n                    if (g[r][c] == 1 && hasRottenNeighbour(g, r, c)) {\n                        next[r][c] = 2;\n                        changed = true;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            if (!changed) break;\n            g = next;\n            minutes++;\n        }\n        for (int[] row : g) {\n            for (int v : row) {\n                if (v == 1) return -1;\n            }\n        }\n        return minutes;\n    }\n\n    private boolean hasRottenNeighbour(int[][] g, int r, int c) {\n        int[][] dirs = {{1,0},{-1,0},{0,1},{0,-1}};\n        for (int[] d : dirs) {\n            int nr = r + d[0], nc = c + d[1];\n            if (nr >= 0 && nc >= 0 && nr < g.length && nc < g[0].length && g[nr][nc] == 2) return true;\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n}",
