      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','`pac` and `atl` are boolean grids.','This step performs one part of the overall transformation. It prepares the state required by the following step and contributes to the final result.','For each top and left cell, `dfs(pac, r, c)`. For each bottom and right cell, `dfs(atl, r, c)`.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.','`dfs(reach, r, c)`: mark the cell. For each unmarked neighbour with height `>=` current, recurse.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.','Collect cells where both are `true`.','This step performs one part of the overall transformation. It prepares the state required by the following step and contributes to the final result.'],
