      algorithm: ['If `endWord` is not in the list, return `0`.','BFS from `beginWord`. For each dequeued word, enqueue every unvisited dictionary word that differs in exactly one letter.','Return the level when `endWord` is dequeued.'],
      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','If `endWord` is not in the list, return `0`.','This is the decision point: evaluate the condition using the state built so far. Taking the correct branch prevents invalid work and keeps the algorithm aligned with the problem\'s constraints.','BFS from `beginWord`. For each dequeued word, enqueue every unvisited dictionary word that differs in exactly one letter.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.','Return the level when `endWord` is dequeued.','This produces the result after the required condition has been established. If the problem guarantees a solution, this final fallback may be unreachable; otherwise it represents the appropriate no-solution case.'],
      correctnessCheck: 'The solution is correct when the maintained state contains exactly the information required by the problem and every processed element has been handled according to the stated rule. The final step reads or constructs the answer from that state.',
      code: "import java.util.ArrayDeque;\nimport java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Queue;\nimport java.util.Set;\n\nclass Solution {\n    public int ladderLength(String beginWord, String endWord, List<String> wordList) {\n        Set<String> words = new HashSet<>(wordList);\n        if (!words.contains(endWord)) return 0;\n        Queue<String> q = new ArrayDeque<>();\n        Set<String> seen = new HashSet<>();\n        q.offer(beginWord);\n        seen.add(beginWord);\n        int level = 1;\n        while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n            for (int size = q.size(); size > 0; size--) {\n                String cur = q.poll();\n                if (cur.equals(endWord)) return level;\n                for (String w : words) {\n                    if (!seen.contains(w) && oneDiff(cur, w)) {\n                        seen.add(w);\n                        q.offer(w);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            level++;\n        }\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    private boolean oneDiff(String a, String b) {\n        int diff = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length(); i++) {\n            if (a.charAt(i) != b.charAt(i) && ++diff > 1) return false;\n        }\n        return diff == 1;\n    }\n}",
