      algorithm: ['Put intervals in a list.','While some pair `(i, j)` overlaps (`a.start <= b.end && b.start <= a.end`), replace `i` with the merged interval and remove `j`.','Sort the result by start for output.'],
      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','Put intervals in a list.','This step performs one part of the overall transformation. It prepares the state required by the following step and contributes to the final result.','While some pair `(i, j)` overlaps (`a.start <= b.end && b.start <= a.end`), replace `i` with the merged interval and remove `j`.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.','Sort the result by start for output.','This produces the result after the required condition has been established. If the problem guarantees a solution, this final fallback may be unreachable; otherwise it represents the appropriate no-solution case.'],
