      algorithm: ['`dist[k] = 0`, others infinity.','Repeat `n - 1` times: for each edge `(u, v, w)`, if `dist[u] + w < dist[v]`, update `dist[v]`.','If any node is unreachable, return `-1`. Otherwise return the maximum distance.'],
      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','`dist[k] = 0`, others infinity.','This step performs one part of the overall transformation. It prepares the state required by the following step and contributes to the final result.','Repeat `n - 1` times: for each edge `(u, v, w)`, if `dist[u] + w < dist[v]`, update `dist[v]`.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.','If any node is unreachable, return `-1`. Otherwise return the maximum distance.','This is the decision point: evaluate the condition using the state built so far. Taking the correct branch prevents invalid work and keeps the algorithm aligned with the problem\'s constraints.'],
      correctnessCheck: 'The solution is correct when the maintained state contains exactly the information required by the problem and every processed element has been handled according to the stated rule. The final step reads or constructs the answer from that state.',
      code: "import java.util.Arrays;\n\nclass Solution {\n    public int networkDelayTime(int[][] times, int n, int k) {\n        int INF = Integer.MAX_VALUE / 2;\n        int[] dist = new int[n + 1];\n        Arrays.fill(dist, INF);\n        dist[k] = 0;\n        for (int round = 0; round < n - 1; round++) {\n            for (int[] e : times) {\n                int u = e[0], v = e[1], w = e[2];\n                if (dist[u] != INF && dist[u] + w < dist[v]) {\n                    dist[v] = dist[u] + w;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        int best = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n            if (dist[i] == INF) return -1;\n            best = Math.max(best, dist[i]);\n        }\n        return best;\n    }\n}",
