      algorithm: ['`zeroSem = 1`, `oddSem = 0`, `evenSem = 0`.','`zero`: for `i` from `1` to `n`: acquire `zeroSem`, print `0`, release `oddSem` if `i` is odd, else `evenSem`.','`odd`: for each odd `i`: acquire `oddSem`, print `i`, release `zeroSem`.','`even`: for each even `i`: acquire `evenSem`, print `i`, release `zeroSem`.'],
      detailedWalkthrough: ['The key is to follow the state of the algorithm from initialization to the final result. The steps below explain not only what to do, but why each operation is useful.','`zeroSem = 1`, `oddSem = 0`, `evenSem = 0`.','This step performs one part of the overall transformation. It prepares the state required by the following step and contributes to the final result.','`zero`: for `i` from `1` to `n`: acquire `zeroSem`, print `0`, release `oddSem` if `i` is odd, else `evenSem`.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.','`odd`: for each odd `i`: acquire `oddSem`, print `i`, release `zeroSem`.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.','`even`: for each even `i`: acquire `evenSem`, print `i`, release `zeroSem`.','The traversal systematically processes the relevant elements or states. Each iteration advances the search or updates the maintained state, so the same work is not needlessly repeated.'],
