    difficulty: 'Hard',
    description: 'Design a data structure for a Least Frequently Used (LFU) cache. Implement `LFUCache`: - `LFUCache(int capacity)` initialises the cache. - `int get(int key)` returns the value if the key exists, otherwise `-1`. A successful `get` increments the key\'s frequency. - `void put(int key, int value)` inserts or updates a key. When the cache is full, evict the key with the lowest frequency. If several keys share that frequency, evict the least recently used among them. An update counts as a use. Both operations must run in $O(1)$ average time.',
    problemIntuition: 'Eviction needs two things: the minimum frequency, and among keys at that frequency, the least recently used. Group keys into buckets by frequency. Each bucket is ordered by recency, so its head is the eviction candidate. Track the current minimum frequency. Then every operation is constant time.',
